Round 16 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
  - `clang/aot/build.c`
  - `clang/runtime/eval_main.c`
- Added AOT allocation-class telemetry:
  - New runtime classes and counters in `aot/_.c`:
    - `APP_FRAME_HEAD`
    - `APP_FRAME_MAT`
    - `DUP_CELL`
    - `CTR_FIELDS`
    - `ENV_BIND`
  - New helper `aot_alloc(size, class)` wraps `heap_alloc` and atomically records calls/nodes when `HVM_AOT_ALLOC=1`.
  - Added `aot_alloc_dump(stderr)`; called from `runtime_eval_main` after evaluation.
  - `aot_env_head` bind-node allocation now uses `aot_alloc(..., ENV_BIND)`.
- Emitted AOT code now attributes explicit allocations:
  - head APP frame pushes -> `AOT_ALLOC_APP_FRAME_HEAD`
  - MAT field APP pushes -> `AOT_ALLOC_APP_FRAME_MAT`
  - DUP env cells (head+expr) -> `AOT_ALLOC_DUP_CELL`
  - ctor payload blocks -> `AOT_ALLOC_CTR_FIELDS`
- Self-tail loop emission refined:
  - Added static scanner `aot_emit_has_self_tail_ref(root, def_id)` over head-position structure.
  - `for(;;)` wrapper is emitted only for defs that actually contain head-tail self `REF`.
  - `continue` in head `REF` is now gated by both self-id and per-def `AOT_EMIT_SELF_LOOP`.
  - Non-self-loop defs emit one-shot `env_cells/env_locs` locals (no loop).
- Fixed `--as-c` temp-path collision bug:
  - Added `aot_build_temp_unique_path(...)` with `pid + atomic seq` suffix.
  - `aot_build_as_c_once` now uses unique `.c` and `.bin` paths.
  - `aot_build_to_output` temp C path also made unique.

Why
- After deopt cleanup, optimization focus is heap behavior; needed direct observability of allocation classes on compiled paths.
- Shared deterministic `--as-c` temp filenames caused parallel runs to corrupt generated C.
- Round 15 loop-wrapped all defs; this round avoids loop/env reset overhead for defs without self-tail recursion.

