Key insight from telemetry
- Even when `AOT_DEOPT=0` and residuals are near-zero, total heap can remain very high.
- `AOT_ALLOC` explains explicit compiled-site allocations, but not all allocations in execution:
  - e.g. `edit_dist` has tiny `AOT_ALLOC` yet huge total heap, implying substantial allocation from non-instrumented paths (generic helpers/interactions or constructors outside current classified sites).
- Immediate next perf work should combine:
  1) broader allocation attribution coverage,
  2) direct compiled-to-compiled call lowering (avoid APP-frame materialization),
  3) mutual/non-tail recursion trampoline/SCC strategy.

